  "interpretation": {
    "overall": "Partial reusable family support, not turnkey T113-i/custom-board enablement. Shared blocks must be checked against the T113-i datasheet and vendor register definitions.",
    "base_io": "Existing shared SoC drivers and pin multiplexing; add board DT for UART0 PB8/PB9, actual supplies, PG RGMII, IRQs and reset/power sequencing.",
    "boot": "DDR initialization is bootloader work. Preserve a verified vendor DRAM initialization path first. Verify PSCI and 2 CPUs online; lack of kernel enable-method by itself is not evidence SMP is unsupported, because bootloader may supply PSCI DT fixups.",
    "storage": "W25N04KW has an explicit SPI-NAND table entry. Linux driver support does not establish BootROM/bootloader support or on-flash format compatibility. Plan ECC, bad blocks, partitioning and UBI/UBIFS.",
    "display": "DE/TCON/DSI/DPHY shared nodes/drivers exist. No TD4322-named panel file found. Port exact panel initialization/power sequencing to DRM panel; identify touch protocol separately. DSI mod clock lookup remains in probe in audited stable tree; assess newer bind-time clock fix. DSI/LVDS mux fix is already present in v6.18.64, unlike base v6.18.",
    "capture": "No T113/D1 entry in sun6i-csi match table or CSI node in common DTS. Existing BT656 support alone does not prove T113 VIN register/DMA compatibility. LT8619C driver absent in upstream 6.18 tree. Rockchip vendor driver is a usable source reference but has private RK dependencies and must be adapted to generic V4L2.",
    "encoding": "Audited Cedrus interface is decode-only; JPEG/MJPEG encoding is missing in stock 6.18.64. Community 6.12.28 encoder patch author reports JPEG on unspecified T113, not verified T113-i/6.18.64. Evaluate V4L2 port before legacy Tina Cedar ABI and userspace libraries.",
    "thermal_restart": "THS driver supports D1 but common T113 DTS lacks THS/thermal integration. Watchdog is reserved. Evaluate upstream T113 thermal DT and watchdog enablement patches for backport, checking T113-i calibration and boot-firmware watchdog ownership.",
    "board_power": "STC8G1K08A board protocol must be implemented and integrated into final kernel poweroff stage; do not cut power from an early userspace shutdown step.",
    "optional": "PWM, analog audio/CVBS, G2D, DSP and auxiliary RISC-V need separate audits if required; no claim of complete support."
  }
}
